judge_raw_output:
The analyzer shows a clear scoring anomaly: quality_score values are far >1 and dominate optimization (max=485,165,195.40979; mean=457,634,869.840732; n_outside_declared_range=31). To prevent wasted budget chasing a buggy scorer, I propose a minimal, reversible objective-level intervention: remove quality_score until its scorer is fixed.

<decision>{
  "failure_location": "implementation",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "The quality_score scorer is producing mis-scaled or overflowed outputs (many values far outside the documented [0,1] range), indicating an implementation/scoring bug rather than optimizer or planning issues.",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "Run diagnostics show quality_score max=485,165,195.40979, mean=457,634,869.840732, and 31/32 values outside the declared [0,1] range; this numeric domination will swamp parameter_spread (mean=0.343545, std=0.039064) despite its weight=0.3. Temporarily dropping the faulty objective stops the optimizer from optimizing an artefact and allows continued progress on the plausible parameter_spread signal.",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {
        "op": "drop",
        "name": "quality_score"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expected_benefit": "Prevents the optimizer from being driven by bogus large quality_score values so that it can meaningfully optimize parameter_spread (currently mean=0.343545, best=0.401328). Should restore sensible selection pressure and let useful improvements (e.g., higher parameter_spread) appear.",
  "validation_plan": "Run iteration 2 with quality_score removed and check that the optimizer progresses on parameter_spread: expect no out-of-range objective dominance, and preferably an increased best or mean parameter_spread relative to iteration 1 (best 0.401328, mean 0.343545). Also monitor population diversity to ensure search doesn't collapse.",
  "confidence": 0.75,
  "target_assessment": {
    "objective": "Dropping the faulty objective is the fastest, lowest-risk way to stop numerical domination and resume useful optimization of parameter_spread.",
    "planning": "Changing planner guidance alone won't stop numeric domination by bad scores and is unlikely to produce an immediate improvement detectable by the validator.",
    "implementation": "Sanitizing or rebuilding the scorer would directly fix the root cause but requires developer work; sanitize_outputs could mark out-of-range values as failed which might harm selection—still credible but riskier than temporarily dropping the objective.",
    "optimization_workflow": "Tuning optimizer params won't fix the underlying bad scores; it only adjusts search behavior against a corrupted objective.",
    "no_change": "Leaving the state unchanged will let the huge, incorrect quality_score values continue to dominate and likely waste budget on artefacts."
  }
}</decision>
